"121_winui_sounded.mst — the Sound Editor, Windows face (WG13).

 The Mac's is `world/77_sounded.mst`: an NSWindow of twelve NSSliders, four
 oscillator rows, and an envelope drawn into an NSImageView by base64 blast.
 THE DOCUMENT IS NOT PORTED, because it never needed porting — `SoundDoc`
 (`world/44b_sounddoc.mst`) is in `world.list` on every platform, holds every
 clamp, and owns the flat parameter contract of
 `docs/asset_editors_design.md` section 3. This file is only a face, and it
 computes nothing about sound that the document does not already know.

 WHAT CHANGED IN THE PORT, and why it is not a downgrade: this is a CELL GRID
 driven by the keyboard, not a panel of sliders. Three reasons, in order of
 weight. A trackbar carries an INTEGER, so twelve sliders over ranges like
 0.0..4.0 means twelve fixed-point mappings and twelve chances to round a
 recipe on the way past. `WM_HSCROLL` is not on the door's allowlist, so
 slider drags would have to be POLLED against the drain's heartbeat — a
 continuous control read discontinuously. And the shell already has a cell
 grid every other view uses, so a keyboard editor is the smaller thing to
 build and the smaller thing to read. Left and right nudge a value; the
 document clamps it, exactly as it clamps a slider.

 THE AUDITION IS THE REAL ONE. `Sound playEffect:` is primitive 263, and it
 renders through the same synth the games use — byte-for-byte upstream's, see
 `win_gui/src/sound/`. It goes out as a doit to the PRIMARY, because only the
 primary holds a game sink, which is the same reason the Mac's editor does it
 that way. No pane is needed: a sound is not a picture.

 EVERY DECISION IS IN A PURE METHOD. `soundDisplayRows` answers rows of
 {text. colour} and touches no window, so the whole display is checkable
 headless — the rule `118_winui_tests.mst` set and the reason its own logic
 could be tested before a pixel existed."

Object subclass: WinShell [
    <classVars: SndDoc SndSel SndPresetIx SndRng SndStatus>

    "── the view ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"

    WinShell class >> soundViewName ^ <Symbol> [ ^#sounded ]
    WinShell class >> soundPaneName ^ <Symbol> [ ^#soundPane ]

    WinShell class >> soundPaneHwnd ^ <Integer> [
        | c |
        c := self controlNamed: self soundPaneName.
        ^c isNil ifTrue: [ 0 ] ifFalse: [ c handle ]
    ]

    WinShell class >> buildSoundPane [
        (self controlNamed: self soundPaneName) ifNotNil: [ :x | ^self ].
        self
            addControl: self soundPaneName
            class: self className
            text: ''
            style: (((WinApi constant: 'WS_CHILD')
                bitOr: (WinApi constant: 'WS_BORDER'))
                bitOr: (WinApi constant: 'WS_CLIPSIBLINGS'))
            exStyle: 0.
        ^self
    ]

    WinShell class >> showSoundPane: aBool <Boolean> [
        (self controlNamed: self soundPaneName) ifNotNil: [ :c | c show: aBool ].
        ^self
    ]

    WinShell class >> layoutSoundPane: content <Array> [
        (self controlNamed: self soundPaneName) ifNotNil: [ :c | c moveTo: content ].
        ^self
    ]

    "── the document ────────────────────────────────────────────────────"

    WinShell class >> soundDoc ^ <Object> [
        "Lazy, and kept for the session — the Mac's editor hides its window
         rather than closing it for the same reason: a recipe you were half way
         through tuning must survive a look at another view."
        SndDoc isNil ifTrue: [ SndDoc := SoundDoc new ].
        ^SndDoc
    ]

    WinShell class >> soundRng ^ <Object> [
        "THE SAME SEED THE MAC USES (77_sounded.mst). `27_random.mst` is an
         exact-integer LCG with a pinned test vector, so Random and Mutate
         produce the identical sequence on both platforms — a free
         cross-platform check that costs one literal."
        SndRng isNil ifTrue: [ SndRng := Random newWithSeed: 20260807 ].
        ^SndRng
    ]

    WinShell class >> soundStatus ^ <String> [
        ^SndStatus isNil ifTrue: [ '' ] ifFalse: [ SndStatus ]
    ]

    WinShell class >> soundStatus: aString <String> [
        SndStatus := aString.
        ^self
    ]

    WinShell class >> soundSel ^ <Integer> [
        ^SndSel isNil ifTrue: [ 1 ] ifFalse: [ SndSel ]
    ]

    WinShell class >> soundPresetIx ^ <Integer> [
        ^SndPresetIx isNil ifTrue: [ -1 ] ifFalse: [ SndPresetIx ]
    ]

    WinShell class >> soundSelect: n <Integer> ^ <Integer> [
        "Clamped against the CURRENT row list, because removing an oscillator
         can leave the selection past the end."
        SndSel := (n max: 1) min: (self soundRows size max: 1).
        ^SndSel
    ]

    "── the editable rows, PURELY ───────────────────────────────────────

     Each entry is {kind. arg. label. lo. hi} — five slots, which is exactly
     what `Array class >> with:` reaches (10_array.mst:173). There is no step
     column: a step is a hundredth of the range, and coarse is ten of those,
     so a range edit cannot leave a step behind disagreeing with it.

     THE BOUNDS ARE THE DOCUMENT'S, not the Mac face's. Its sliders stop at
     1.0 for attack where SoundDoc clamps at 2.0, and at 2000 Hz for a sweep
     the model takes to 4000 — so a preset can sit outside its own slider and
     the next drag silently truncates the recipe. Reading the model's real
     bounds costs nothing and cannot do that."

    WinShell class >> soundFields ^ <OrderedCollection> [
        | out |
        out := OrderedCollection new.
        out add: (Array with: #param with: #duration   with: 'duration'   with: 0.05 with: 4.0).
        out add: (Array with: #param with: #attack     with: 'attack'     with: 0.0  with: 2.0).
        out add: (Array with: #param with: #decay      with: 'decay'      with: 0.0  with: 2.0).
        out add: (Array with: #param with: #sustain    with: 'sustain'    with: 0.0  with: 1.0).
        out add: (Array with: #param with: #release    with: 'release'    with: 0.0  with: 2.0).
        out add: (Array with: #param with: #sweepStart with: 'sweep from' with: 0.0  with: 4000.0).
        out add: (Array with: #param with: #sweepEnd   with: 'sweep to'   with: 0.0  with: 4000.0).
        out add: (Array with: #param with: #noiseMix   with: 'noise'      with: 0.0  with: 1.0).
        out add: (Array with: #param with: #distortion with: 'distortion' with: 0.0  with: 3.0).
        out add: (Array with: #param with: #echoCount  with: 'echoes'     with: 0    with: 8).
        out add: (Array with: #param with: #echoDelay  with: 'echo delay' with: 0.0  with: 0.5).
        out add: (Array with: #param with: #echoDecay  with: 'echo decay' with: 0.0  with: 1.0).
        out add: (Array with: #param with: #seed       with: 'seed'       with: 1    with: 99999).
        ^out
    ]

    WinShell class >> soundRows ^ <OrderedCollection> [
        "The recipe fields, then three fields per LIVE oscillator. The list
         shrinks and grows with `Osc +`/`Osc -`, which is why the selection is
         clamped against it rather than remembered as a coordinate."
        | out doc i |
        out := self soundFields.
        doc := self soundDoc.
        i := 1.
        [ i <= doc oscCount ] whileTrue: [
            out add: (Array with: #oscWave with: i with: 'osc ' , i printString , ' wave'
                            with: 0 with: 5).
            out add: (Array with: #oscFreq with: i with: 'osc ' , i printString , ' freq'
                            with: 20.0 with: 8000.0).
            out add: (Array with: #oscAmp with: i with: 'osc ' , i printString , ' amp'
                            with: 0.0 with: 1.0).
            out add: (Array with: #oscPw with: i with: 'osc ' , i printString , ' width'
                            with: 0.01 with: 0.99).
            i := i + 1 ].
        ^out
    ]

    WinShell class >> soundValueOf: field <Array> ^ <Number> [
        | kind arg doc |
        kind := field at: 1.
        arg := field at: 2.
        doc := self soundDoc.
        kind == #param ifTrue: [ ^doc perform: arg ].
        kind == #oscWave ifTrue: [ ^(doc oscAt: arg) at: 1 ].
        kind == #oscFreq ifTrue: [ ^(doc oscAt: arg) at: 2 ].
        kind == #oscAmp ifTrue: [ ^(doc oscAt: arg) at: 3 ].
        kind == #oscPw ifTrue: [ ^(doc oscAt: arg) at: 5 ].
        ^0
    ]

    WinShell class >> soundSet: field <Array> to: v <Number> [
        "Every write goes through the DOCUMENT's setter, so the document's
         clamp is the only clamp — section 3's rule, `the native side never
         truncates`, read from the other end."
        | kind arg doc |
        kind := field at: 1.
        arg := field at: 2.
        doc := self soundDoc.
        kind == #param ifTrue: [
            ^doc perform: (arg , ':') asSymbol with: v ].
        kind == #oscWave ifTrue: [ ^doc osc: arg wave: v rounded ].
        kind == #oscFreq ifTrue: [ ^doc osc: arg freq: v ].
        kind == #oscAmp ifTrue: [ ^doc osc: arg amp: v ].
        kind == #oscPw ifTrue: [ ^doc osc: arg pw: v ].
        ^self
    ]

    WinShell class >> soundShow: field <Array> ^ <String> [
        "What a value READS as. The units are part of the reading — `0.3` and
         `0.3 s` are the same number and different facts."
        | kind arg v |
        kind := field at: 1.
        arg := field at: 2.
        v := self soundValueOf: field.
        kind == #oscWave ifTrue: [ ^self soundDoc oscWaveNameAt: arg ].
        kind == #oscFreq ifTrue: [ ^v rounded printString , ' Hz' ].
        (arg == #seed or: [ arg == #echoCount ]) ifTrue: [ ^v rounded printString ].
        (arg == #sweepStart or: [ arg == #sweepEnd ])
            ifTrue: [ ^v rounded printString , ' Hz' ].
        (arg == #duration or: [ arg == #echoDelay ])
            ifTrue: [ ^(self sndRound2: v) , ' s' ].
        ^self sndRound2: v
    ]

    WinShell class >> sndRound2: v <Number> ^ <String> [
        ^((v * 100) rounded / 100.0) printString
    ]

    WinShell class >> soundBarFor: field <Array> ^ <String> [
        "Twenty cells of where this value sits in its range. A number tells you
         what it is; the bar tells you what is LEFT, which is the question a
         hand on a slider is really asking."
        | lo hi v n out i |
        lo := field at: 4.
        hi := field at: 5.
        v := self soundValueOf: field.
        n := hi > lo
            ifTrue: [ (((v - lo) / (hi - lo) * 20) rounded max: 0) min: 20 ]
            ifFalse: [ 0 ].
        out := ''.
        i := 0.
        [ i < 20 ] whileTrue: [
            out := out , (i < n ifTrue: [ '#' ] ifFalse: [ '.' ]).
            i := i + 1 ].
        ^out
    ]

    "── the display, PURELY ─────────────────────────────────────────────"

    WinShell class >> soundDisplayRows ^ <OrderedCollection> [
        | out doc rows sel field label |
        out := OrderedCollection new.
        doc := self soundDoc.
        rows := self soundRows.
        sel := (self soundSel max: 1) min: rows size.
        out add: (Array with: 'SOUND EDITOR   ' , doc name , '   preset: '
                             , self soundPresetLabel with: 16r000000).
        out add: (Array with: '' with: 16r000000).
        1 to: rows size do: [ :i |
            field := rows at: i.
            label := self padded: (field at: 3) to: 12.
            out add: (Array
                with: (i = sel ifTrue: [ '> ' ] ifFalse: [ '  ' ])
                    , label , ' '
                    , (self padded: (self soundShow: field) to: 10)
                    , ' ' , (self soundBarFor: field)
                with: (i = sel ifTrue: [ 16r0000C0 ] ifFalse: [ 16r000000 ])) ].
        out add: (Array with: '' with: 16r000000).
        out add: (Array with: 'up/down pick   left/right nudge   shift = x10'
                        with: 16r606060).
        out add: (Array with: 'P play   [ ] preset   R random   M mutate'
                        with: 16r606060).
        out add: (Array with: 'N new    + - oscillators   S save as a sheet'
                        with: 16r606060).
        self soundStatus isEmpty ifFalse: [
            out add: (Array with: '' with: 16r000000).
            out add: (Array with: self soundStatus with: 16r806000) ].
        ^out
    ]

    WinShell class >> soundPresetLabel ^ <String> [
        | ix |
        ix := self soundPresetIx.
        (ix < 0 or: [ ix > 11 ]) ifTrue: [ ^'-' ].
        ^SoundDoc presetNames at: ix + 1
    ]

    "── the blit ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"

    WinShell class >> renderSound ^ <Boolean> [
        | hwnd cw ch c r cols rows base row col |
        hwnd := self soundPaneHwnd.
        hwnd = 0 ifTrue: [ ^false ].
        (WinRender cellWidthFor: hwnd) = 0 ifTrue: [
            (WinRender attach: hwnd points: 9 dpi: self editorMetricsDpi)
                ifFalse: [ ^false ] ].
        cw := WinRender cellWidthFor: hwnd.
        ch := WinRender cellHeightFor: hwnd.
        (cw = 0 or: [ ch = 0 ]) ifTrue: [ ^false ].
        c := self controlNamed: self soundPaneName.
        r := [ c screenRect ] on: Error do: [ :e | nil ].
        r isNil ifTrue: [ ^false ].
        cols := ((((r at: 3) - (r at: 1)) // cw) max: 1).
        rows := ((((r at: 4) - (r at: 2)) // ch) max: 1).
        base := WinRender gridFor: hwnd cols: cols rows: rows.
        base = 0 ifTrue: [ ^false ].
        WinRender clear: hwnd to: 16r000000 on: 16rFFFFFF.
        row := 0.
        "`col` is a METHOD temp deliberately — declared inside the outer block
         it reads as nil in the inner one, which cost an afternoon in 118."
        self soundDisplayRows do: [ :pair |
            row < rows ifTrue: [
                col := 0.
                (pair at: 1) do: [ :chr |
                    col < cols ifTrue: [
                        WinRender at: base col: col row: row cols: cols
                            put: (chr asInteger < 32 ifTrue: [ 32 ] ifFalse: [ chr asInteger ])
                            fg: (pair at: 2)
                            bg: 16rFFFFFF ].
                    col := col + 1 ].
                row := row + 1 ] ].
        WinRender caretFor: hwnd col: 0 row: 0 visible: false.
        ^WinRender present: hwnd
    ]

    "── input ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"

    WinShell class >> soundMessage: msg <Integer> wParam: wp <Integer> lParam: lp <Integer> ^ <Object> [
        ^[ self soundMessageBody: msg wParam: wp lParam: lp ]
            on: Error do: [ :e | PaintError := e messageText. #defwindowproc ]
    ]

    WinShell class >> soundMessageBody: msg <Integer> wParam: wp <Integer> lParam: lp <Integer> ^ <Object> [
        msg = (WinApi constant: 'WM_LBUTTONDOWN') ifTrue: [
            WinApi setFocus: self soundPaneHwnd.
            ^self soundClickAt: lp ].
        msg = (WinApi constant: 'WM_KEYDOWN') ifTrue: [ ^self soundKeyDown: wp ].
        msg = (WinApi constant: 'WM_CHAR') ifTrue: [ ^self soundChar: wp ].
        ^#defwindowproc
    ]

    WinShell class >> soundClickAt: lp <Integer> ^ <Object> [
        "A click picks the row under it. The first two lines are the title and
         a blank, so the field list starts at row 2 counting from zero."
        | hwnd ch y rows |
        hwnd := self soundPaneHwnd.
        hwnd = 0 ifTrue: [ ^0 ].
        ch := WinRender cellHeightFor: hwnd.
        ch = 0 ifTrue: [ ^0 ].
        y := (self hiWordSigned: lp) // ch.
        rows := self soundRows size.
        (y >= 2 and: [ y - 1 <= rows ]) ifTrue: [
            SndSel := y - 1.
            self renderSound ].
        ^0
    ]

    WinShell class >> soundKeyDown: vk <Integer> ^ <Object> [
        | rows |
        rows := self soundRows size.
        vk = 16r26 ifTrue: [                          "VK_UP"
            SndSel := ((self soundSel) - 1 max: 1).
            self renderSound. ^0 ].
        vk = 16r28 ifTrue: [                          "VK_DOWN"
            SndSel := ((self soundSel) + 1 min: rows).
            self renderSound. ^0 ].
        vk = 16r25 ifTrue: [ ^self soundNudge: -1 ].  "VK_LEFT"
        vk = 16r27 ifTrue: [ ^self soundNudge: 1 ].   "VK_RIGHT"
        ^#defwindowproc
    ]

    WinShell class >> soundChar: code <Integer> ^ <Object> [
        | ch |
        code < 32 ifTrue: [ ^#defwindowproc ].
        ch := (Character value: code) asUppercase.
        ch = $P ifTrue: [ ^self soundPlay ].
        ch = $R ifTrue: [ ^self soundRandom ].
        ch = $M ifTrue: [ ^self soundMutate ].
        ch = $N ifTrue: [ ^self soundNew ].
        ch = $S ifTrue: [ ^self soundSave ].
        ch = $] ifTrue: [ ^self soundPreset: self soundPresetIx + 1 ].
        ch = $[ ifTrue: [ ^self soundPreset: self soundPresetIx - 1 ].
        ch = $+ ifTrue: [ ^self soundAddOsc ].
        ch = $= ifTrue: [ ^self soundAddOsc ].
        ch = $- ifTrue: [ ^self soundRemoveOsc ].
        ^#defwindowproc
    ]

    WinShell class >> soundNudge: dir <Integer> ^ <Object> [
        "A hundredth of the range, or a tenth with Shift held. Wave and echo
         count step by whole numbers instead — six waves and nine echo counts
         are not a continuum, and a hundredth of them is nothing."
        | rows field lo hi step v |
        rows := self soundRows.
        rows isEmpty ifTrue: [ ^0 ].
        field := rows at: ((self soundSel max: 1) min: rows size).
        lo := field at: 4.
        hi := field at: 5.
        ((field at: 1) == #oscWave or: [ (field at: 2) == #echoCount ])
            ifTrue: [ step := 1 ]
            ifFalse: [
                step := (hi - lo) / 100.0.
                self shiftIsDown ifTrue: [ step := step * 10 ] ].
        v := (self soundValueOf: field) + (step * dir).
        self soundSet: field to: v.
        SndPresetIx := -1.
        self soundStatus: ''.
        self renderSound.
        ^0
    ]

    "── the verbs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────"

    WinShell class >> soundPlay ^ <Object> [
        "THE REAL SYNTH. Primitive 263 renders the recipe and plays it; the
         doit goes to the PRIMARY because only the primary holds a game sink.
         `paramsList printString` is a literal array, so the wire text parses
         on the far side with nothing to encode or escape."
        | doc |
        doc := self soundDoc.
        Worker uiDoit: 'Sound playEffect: ' , doc paramsList printString
            onReply: [ :r | ].
        self soundStatus: 'played (' , doc oscCount printString , ' osc, seed '
            , doc seed printString , ')'.
        self renderSound.
        ^0
    ]

    WinShell class >> soundPreset: ix <Integer> ^ <Object> [
        | n |
        n := ix \\ 12.
        SndPresetIx := n.
        self soundDoc loadPreset: n.
        self soundStatus: ''.
        self renderSound.
        ^self soundPlay
    ]

    WinShell class >> soundRandom ^ <Object> [
        self soundDoc randomize: self soundRng.
        SndPresetIx := -1.
        self soundStatus: ''.
        self renderSound.
        ^self soundPlay
    ]

    WinShell class >> soundMutate ^ <Object> [
        "Nudge, don't reroll — the document's own word for it. The preset name
         is KEPT: a mutated coin is still recognisably the coin, which is the
         whole reason the verb exists next to Random."
        self soundDoc mutate: self soundRng.
        self soundStatus: ''.
        self renderSound.
        ^self soundPlay
    ]

    WinShell class >> soundNew ^ <Object> [
        SndDoc := SoundDoc new.
        SndPresetIx := -1.
        SndSel := 1.
        self soundStatus: 'a fresh 440Hz sine'.
        self renderSound.
        ^0
    ]

    WinShell class >> soundAddOsc ^ <Object> [
        self soundDoc addOsc
            ifTrue: [ self soundStatus: '' ]
            ifFalse: [ self soundStatus: 'four oscillators is the stack' ].
        self renderSound.
        ^0
    ]

    WinShell class >> soundRemoveOsc ^ <Object> [
        self soundDoc removeOsc
            ifTrue: [ SndSel := (self soundSel min: self soundRows size) max: 1 ]
            ifFalse: [ self soundStatus: 'one oscillator stays' ].
        self renderSound.
        ^0
    ]

    WinShell class >> soundSave ^ <Object> [
        "Saves as SOURCE in the image, the same write path the Browser's Accept
         takes — a sound sheet is an ordinary class carrying an `isSoundSheet`
         marker and a `params` array, so `Laser play` works from a Workspace
         and from a game with nothing else installed."
        | doc reply |
        doc := self soundDoc.
        (SpriteDoc validName: doc name) ifFalse: [
            self soundStatus: 'save: name must be a capitalised identifier'.
            self renderSound.
            ^0 ].
        reply := [ WinHost persistClass: doc sheetSource ]
            on: Error do: [ :e | Array with: false with: e messageText ].
        self soundStatus: ((reply at: 1)
            ifTrue: [ 'saved ' , doc name ]
            ifFalse: [ 'save FAILED: ' , (reply at: 2) printString ]).
        self renderSound.
        ^0
    ]

    "── the scripted surface ────────────────────────────────────────────
     What a headless harness drives, and what the Mac's own stage-6 gate
     drives on its side: pick a preset, read the recipe back, round-trip it."

    WinShell class >> sndStatus ^ <String> [ ^self soundStatus ]
    WinShell class >> sndParams ^ <String> [ ^self soundDoc paramsList printString ]
    WinShell class >> sndName ^ <String> [ ^self soundDoc name ]
    WinShell class >> sndDocLoad: params <Array> ^ <String> [
        ^(self soundDoc fromParams: params) printString
    ]
]
